    "reason": "The Japanese word 勧告 (kankoku) refers to a formal recommendation or warning, often from an authority or official body. It is much narrower and more formal than the general English 'advice'. It would be unnatural for a learner to use 勧告 for everyday advice. More common and natural equivalents for general 'advice' include 助言 (jogen) or アドバイス (adobaisu).",
